validate/linked_ld.jl — running log (2026-11-15). Hypotheses are written before each test.
Criteria: validate/linked_ld_criteria.md (committed before any comparison on fresh data, H′).
Development data: D, F, G of linked_decay/linked_source (all previously seen; disclosed).

== 1. Stage accounting of Σ_l Y_l² on D, F, G (stage-instrumented re-runs, same seeds as linked_decay/linked_source; 39 + 48 + 66 runs, 3039 thread-s) ==

Instrumentation (`stage`): per generation from MOVE − 60 to MOVE + 99, per locus Y_l = Cov(B_l, x_l)
at adults (A), π-weighted adults (Π, deterministic selection), survivors (S; plus E[ΣŶ²|adults]
over 16 Bernoulli(π) redraws with an own RNG), the survivors' expected gamete pool (Gp, exact under
QTSim's single crossover: Y^Gp = Y^S − Cov_S(R,x) + Z, R_l = Σ_k ρ_kl x_k), offspring before
mutation (O), next adults (after mutation). Check: V_G bitwise identical to simulate; Σ Y² at A
equals linked_source's Σ yY on the same run.

Hypotheses before looking:
 (i)  the exact first-order expectations (survival MC, (1 − 3ε)ΣY² + εΣμ22 for each sampling stage,
      Σ(Y − CovRx)² + Σ(v Var R + CovRx²)/(2n) for recombination, mutation Σ[(L−1)m v + m Var B]/(2N))
      reproduce the measured mean stage changes;
 (ii) the recursion's recombination stage (P ← RPR) misses the cross-chromosome part ρZ of the
      gamete: its random-pairing variance (seeding mostly the loosely linked classes) and the
      between-chromosome association created by selection, which recombination transmits in full
      (the recursion attenuates selection's change by 1 − ρ): expected to be the main shortfall;
 (iii) the sampling stages: the recursion's Var(B)v differs from the exact μ22 by H (minor);
 (iv) mutation: the recursion omits the Σ_{k≠l} m_k v_l term (minor);
 (v)  selection: Bulmer's step agrees with the π pass before the move to within ~20%.


