Columns (per generation, ÷ mean Σ Y² at the adults): sel_meas = π pass − adults (exact deterministic
selection); sel_recur = y_step!'s Bulmer step at the adults' state; sel_bul without its
linearisation; sel_ind with 1/(ω² + V_P); sel_full with the cumulant terms b κ(B,x,G) (sel_k3) and
(b² − 1/S)κ(B,x,G,G)/2 (sel_k4); surv_exact = E over 16 Bernoulli(π) redraws; surv_first =
(1 − 3ε)ΣY² + εΣμ22 − ΣY²; rec_recur = Σ(Y − Cov(R,x))² − ΣY² (P ← RPR with exact pairwise ρ),
rec_recurb with the classes' ρ̄; rec_theory adds the pairing noise Σ(v Var R + Cov(R,x)²)/(2n), the
pairing mean and the between-chromosome association created by selection, −Cov(R,G)Cov(x,G)/S_c;
rec_exact uses the measured π-weighted between association instead (it double-counts the adults'
own pairing noise, hence too high); off_exact = (1 − 3/M)ΣY_Gp² + Σμ22/M − ΣY_Gp²; mut_exact =
Σ[(L − 1)m v + m Var B]/(2N).

Reading (development):
 (i) holds: the measured stage changes close (total ≈ 0 before the move), and each is reproduced by
     its exact first-order expectation: survival by the redraws (+0.0117 vs +0.0110 on D), recombination
     by rec_theory (D −0.0675 vs −0.0674, F −0.0760 vs −0.0768, G −0.0818 vs −0.0820), offspring
     sampling by (1 − 3/M)Y² + μ22/M, mutation by its two terms (negligible: ~1e-4).
 (ii) holds in direction, not in size: at the measured state the old recombination step over-decays
     Σ Y² by 0.005 (D), 0.009 (F), 0.011 (G) per generation (÷ΣY²): the pairing noise (+0.012..0.013)
     outweighs the between-chromosome association created by selection (−0.008..−0.011). The class
     binning of ρ adds −0.0015.
 (iii) survival: the recursion's ε Var(B)v is 0.002 below the exact (H, Bernoulli ε) on D, ≈ 0 on F.
 (iv) mutation: negligible either way.
 (v) selection: before the move Bulmer's step over-decays by 0.006 (D), 0.0013 (F), 0.0023 (G);
     1/(ω² + V_P) and the fourth-cumulant term remove about two thirds. Under the move the directional
     third-cumulant term b κ(B,x,G) adds +0.015 (D 0..49), +0.011 (G): the recursion, which drops it,
     over-decays Σ Y² by 0.025 there.
 So at the measured state the per-generation imbalance of the old recursion is only −0.012 (D, F, G
 before the move), yet its stationary Σ E[yY] is 0.6–0.9 of measured: the Σ Y² view hides where the
 error is. Next: the same accounting in the recursion's own class space.

== 2. Class-space stage accounting on D (per locus the class vector y_l, s = partner bin × split class; 39 runs, 7066 thread-s) ==

Instrumentation (`class`): per locus the class sums B_{l,s} and ρ-weighted sums R_{l,s} of every
chromosome by prefix sums over contiguous class segments; y_l at A, Π, S, the gamete pool, O; the
recursion's stage map applied per locus to the measured class vectors at the start of each stage,
the sampling seeds and the pairing noise as class matrices; summaries Σ_l (Σ_s y)² and by blocks of
split classes (tight: ρ < 0.01, classes 1–3; loose: 4–7).
Hypotheses before looking: the shortfall is in the tightly linked block (80% of Σ Y²), through its
slow turnover; the recombination and selection errors of section 1 sit in the loose block.


