Reading: the tight block is balanced in both (−0.0005 vs −0.0003): the first hypothesis is false.
The between + pairing correction makes the recombination step exact in every block (TL +0.0322 vs
+0.0323, LL −0.0953 vs −0.0947). With it the recursion is balanced at the measured state to
−0.006 (selection −0.0033, survival −0.0013 in LL). Yet section 4 (below) shows the corrected
recursion's stationary state barely moves. So the error is not in a per-locus stage map: it is in
how the recursion carries the moments summed over loci.

== 3. The recursion iterated from the full measured class moments (D; 39 short runs, ~200 thread-s) ==

`pm` measures P_st = Σ_{l∈a} y_{l,s} y_{l,t} and m_s per group at 12 generations before the move;
the recursion is iterated from the measured (m, P) with the run's pre-move drivers.
Hypothesis before looking: if the per-locus stage maps are right, the recursion started at the
measured state stays there (Σ P within a few per cent over 500 generations).
Result (Σ P / measured after 1, 10, 50, 500 generations; level B as in linked_decay):
  01192 0.95 0.76 0.61 0.56 | 00854 0.86 0.55 0.46 0.44 | 07594 0.94 0.74 0.58 0.51 | 14110 0.97 0.87 0.76 0.67
  12000 0.93 0.77 0.68 0.67 | 05562 0.96 0.87 0.82 0.80 | 09697 0.96 0.90 0.85 0.82 | (06159, L = 100: rises to 1.8)
It falls by up to 14% in ONE generation (00854), in the loose block and the tight × loose block.
Decomposing that generation: the matrix form of the selection step gives −0.173 of Σ P for 00854
where the per-locus form (section 2) gives +0.015. The only difference is one approximation in
y_step!: the cross term of the mean LD with Bulmer's offset, Σ_l A E[y_l] b_lᵀ with b_l = −c v_l/S,
is written v̄ A m bᵀ/v̄ (Σ_l E[y_l] v_l ≈ v̄ m: averaging over loci before the product). But both the
mean LD and the offset are ∝ v_l (under the recursion itself E[y_l] = (I − A)⁻¹(−c/S) v_l exactly),
so Σ_l E[y_l] v_l = (Σv²/Σv) m, and Σv²/Σv = v̄(1 + CV²) is several times v̄ when the loci's
variances are unequal (as they are: few segregating loci carry most of the variance). The term is
positive (the mean LD and the offset are both negative), so the old recursion under-weights it.
With the weight Σv²/Σv (`vhet`; matrix step for 00854 −0.007 vs per-locus +0.015, 14110 −0.037 vs
−0.037) the iteration from the measured state stays at 0.84–1.16 after 500 generations
(01192 1.16, 04943 1.58, 00854 0.95, 06004 1.12, 09697 0.92, 14110 0.76, 07594 0.86, 12000 0.89,
14771 1.00, 01925 0.84, 12463 0.91, 05562 0.88; 06159 1.9).
Diagnosis: the shortfall of E[y_s y_t] is carried by the selection stage, through the
heterogeneity among loci of Bulmer's step (a Jensen gap in the summed moments), not by drift
seeding (the class covariances Σ_B match the exact Σ_l v_l Cov(B_ls, B_lt) to 0–25% per block, total
1.00) nor by the binning. The recombination step's missing cross-chromosome terms are real but
nearly cancel in the stationary state (+1–2% of Σ E[yY]); the directional third-cumulant term
(dropped) explains what remains under the move.

== 4. The corrected recursion driven by the runs (development on D, G, F) ==

Variants (`yfix_step!`): B0 = linked_decay's level B; Bv = `vhet` only; Bx = between + pairing +
mutfull + sind (no vhet); Bs = all five (level B*); Bp0 = linked_source's B′; Bps = B′ with all five
(level B′*). Hypothesis before looking: Bs brings Σ E[yY] to within 10% of measured before the move
and within 20% in 50..99; B′* raises H substantially (H is seeded by 2εP) without spoiling K.

