Reading. The diagnosis is confirmed where it was aimed: correcting the heterogeneity weight of
Bulmer's step (and the four small exact terms) removes the shortfall of the allele–background LD on
fresh inputs (0.78 → 0.97 before the move, 0.74 → 0.90 under it; the remaining ~10% in 50..99 is
the dropped directional third-cumulant term, measured at +0.01–0.015 of Σ Y² per generation in
section 1). It also lifts the variance heterogeneity H from 0.38 to 0.71 before the move. It does
not fix the closed association: on H′, as on G, ΣC and the cumulative loss are off (the loss is now
overpredicted by e^0.47 = 1.6×) and the source K under the move is 1.5× measured, for B′ and B′*
alike. With y right, the remaining defects of the source are in H under the move (0.49) and in the
dropped directional terms of K (βκ₅, which make the measured K fall late in the move) — not in y.
The exploratory driven-spectrum check was not run ((c) failed, as the task prescribes).
